  "text": {
    "tagline": "Low-end infrastructure for medium and large businesses.",
    "blurb": "Lowfold's first release as a limited company. Ten basses for the sound recorder synths: wobble, growl, sub, reese and organ bass, built for UK garage, 2-step, speed garage and the heavy stuff after midnight.",
    "intro": [
      "Bass Enterprise Edition is LFS012, the twelfth Lowfold release and the first since we became a proper company with a registered office and a fax machine.",
      "It holds {count} bass presets for the sound recorder synths. Wobbles, growls, subs, a reese and an organ bass. They were built for 2-step and speed garage at 130 to 140 and tested on a rig in a railway arch."
    ],
    "maker_note": [
      "We started Lowfold on a pirate frequency in 1995. We are now Lowfold Sound System Ltd. The accountant says this is progress. The neighbours disagree.",
      "Big up the arch, the late shift and anyone still carrying dubplates on the night bus.",
      "Dez and Tash, Directors"
    ],
    "install": [
      "Insert the disc. In the Library tab it appears as LFS012CD.",
      "Open the Bass folder. Double-click a preset to load it.",
      "Turn the subs up. Then down a bit. Neighbours."
    ],
    "license": [
      "LICENCE",
      "Lowfold Sound System Ltd licenses you to use these presets on one computer. Tracks you make with them are yours. No royalties. No paperwork.",
      "You may not copy this disc or sell the presets as a sound library. All rights of the producer and of the owner of the work reserved.",
      "Lowfold Sound System Ltd accepts no liability for damage to speakers, windows or tenancy agreements."
    ],
